# Development Principles

## How to work

- **TDD first** — failing spec before production code per slice; red → green → refactor.
- **Rails way** — MVC, REST, existing gestor patterns; no extra layers unless the slice needs them.
- **Small pieces** — vertical slices, shippable independently.
- **Think before coding** — state assumptions; ask when uncertain; surface tradeoffs.
- **Simplicity first** — minimum code that solves the problem; no speculative features or abstractions.
- **Surgical changes** — touch only what the request requires; match existing style; don't refactor unrelated code.
- **Verifiable goals** — define success criteria up front (e.g. "spec fails, then passes").

## Architecture principles

- **KISS / YAGNI** — standard CRUD until complexity demands extraction.
- **SRP** — models persist; controllers orchestrate HTTP; services hold business logic; views display.
- **Skinny everything** — delegate beyond simple CRUD to services; keep models thin.
- **Callbacks** — only for data normalization (`before_validation`, `before_save`). Side effects (emails, jobs, APIs) belong in services.
- **Explicit over implicit** — named service calls over hidden callback chains.
- **No premature abstraction** — extract after 3+ concrete repetitions, not on the first case.

## Quality gates

- Run RuboCop on touched Ruby: `docker compose exec web bundle exec rubocop`
- Co-locate tests with the layer changed (`spec/models`, `spec/requests`, `spec/services`, etc.)
- Smallest diff that solves the problem; no unrelated edits.
